# VisualWeaver per-machine overrides. Copy to .visualweaver.env (gitignored) and
# uncomment what you need. A real environment variable always wins over this file.
#
# The web UI listens on ALL network interfaces by default, so other devices on
# your network can reach it. VisualWeaver has no built-in authentication: on an
# untrusted network, restrict it to this machine only:
#VISUALWEAVER_HOST=127.0.0.1
#
# Web UI port (default 8420) and the dedicated Redis port (default 6389):
#VISUALWEAVER_PORT=8420
#VISUALWEAVER_REDIS_PORT=6389
#
# Interpreter for the virtualenv (install.sh normally picks the newest supported):
#PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.12
